[{:db/id 17592186119832 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d60eaae3-858a-5d2f-83b8-ccadfd1429d3"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119833 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-34ca6320-0524-59fc-8f68-7b8524566ac6"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119835 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-fc9c30e8-905e-5cc3-9596-440fe740820a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-d60eaae3-858a-5d2f-83b8-ccadfd1429d3" :question/id #uuid "d60eaae3-858a-5d2f-83b8-ccadfd1429d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-330499" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(-1,3,2)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=⟨4,0,1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of the point $P$ is $p=⟨-1,3,2⟩$ and the normal vector of the plane is $n=⟨4,0,1⟩.$\n\nUsing the dot product we can find an equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨4,0,1⟩ & =⟨-1,3,2⟩\\cdot ⟨4,0,1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨4,0,1⟩ & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨4,0,1⟩ & =-2 \\\\ 4x+z & =-2 \\\\ 4x+z+2 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-261a61c5-5d9c-5e73-a9c8-99e605e6c3e7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-261a61c5-5d9c-5e73-a9c8-99e605e6c3e7" :answer-field/id #uuid "261a61c5-5d9c-5e73-a9c8-99e605e6c3e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a34b8674-3166-5800-b2b6-3d8e2d749e97" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cf32c54e-7d9c-57e0-ac44-14a3df665bca" "answer-a34b8674-3166-5800-b2b6-3d8e2d749e97" "answer-9f69fd47-a1f5-5770-8c3d-1d9916854264" "answer-2717e35a-d5d8-5b8d-b82d-51c22326e847" "answer-bb1a451c-30a6-598a-a1e4-37120fd4f9f8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cf32c54e-7d9c-57e0-ac44-14a3df665bca" :answer/id #uuid "cf32c54e-7d9c-57e0-ac44-14a3df665bca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4x+y+z+2=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a34b8674-3166-5800-b2b6-3d8e2d749e97" :answer/id #uuid "a34b8674-3166-5800-b2b6-3d8e2d749e97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4x+z+2=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f69fd47-a1f5-5770-8c3d-1d9916854264" :answer/id #uuid "9f69fd47-a1f5-5770-8c3d-1d9916854264" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4x+z-2=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2717e35a-d5d8-5b8d-b82d-51c22326e847" :answer/id #uuid "2717e35a-d5d8-5b8d-b82d-51c22326e847" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4x-y+z+2=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bb1a451c-30a6-598a-a1e4-37120fd4f9f8" :answer/id #uuid "bb1a451c-30a6-598a-a1e4-37120fd4f9f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+4y+z+2=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-34ca6320-0524-59fc-8f68-7b8524566ac6" :question/id #uuid "34ca6320-0524-59fc-8f68-7b8524566ac6" :question/math-academy-id "q-70815" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(0,0,3)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n${\\begin{aligned}x=2+2t \\\\ y=5t \\\\ z=1-t\\end{aligned}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨0,0,3⟩.$ From the parametrical equation, we find that the line is parallel to the vector $⟨2,5,-1⟩.$ So, the normal vector of the plane is \n\n$$\nn=⟨2,5,-1⟩.\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,5,-1⟩ & =⟨0,0,3⟩\\cdot ⟨2,5,-1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,5,-1⟩ & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨2,5,-1⟩ & =-3 \\\\ 2x+5y-z & =-3 \\\\ 2x+5y-z+3 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f6c20a87-b8c2-530d-b3e1-fb8bd507d26c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f6c20a87-b8c2-530d-b3e1-fb8bd507d26c" :answer-field/id #uuid "f6c20a87-b8c2-530d-b3e1-fb8bd507d26c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2493b28e-9805-515c-9bb7-52400b1ebad9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d4795ff7-792e-54da-b148-8c4ee1d289d5" "answer-2493b28e-9805-515c-9bb7-52400b1ebad9" "answer-d3c26dd6-942b-51e3-9221-ce5b6eff63d3" "answer-a11ad414-7674-5c26-950f-59f6a219f5d2" "answer-5c7649c7-0f92-5513-b462-907271b682a9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d4795ff7-792e-54da-b148-8c4ee1d289d5" :answer/id #uuid "d4795ff7-792e-54da-b148-8c4ee1d289d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x+5y+z-4=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2493b28e-9805-515c-9bb7-52400b1ebad9" :answer/id #uuid "2493b28e-9805-515c-9bb7-52400b1ebad9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x+5y-z+3=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d3c26dd6-942b-51e3-9221-ce5b6eff63d3" :answer/id #uuid "d3c26dd6-942b-51e3-9221-ce5b6eff63d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x+5y-z-4=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a11ad414-7674-5c26-950f-59f6a219f5d2" :answer/id #uuid "a11ad414-7674-5c26-950f-59f6a219f5d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x-z+3=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5c7649c7-0f92-5513-b462-907271b682a9" :answer/id #uuid "5c7649c7-0f92-5513-b462-907271b682a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3z+3=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-fc9c30e8-905e-5cc3-9596-440fe740820a" :question/id #uuid "fc9c30e8-905e-5cc3-9596-440fe740820a" :question/math-academy-id "q-128410" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the points $A(1,-2,1)$, $P(3,-1,2)$ and $Q(4,2,0).$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $A,P$ and $Q$ are $a=⟨1,-2,1⟩,\\,p=⟨3,-1,2⟩,$ and $q=⟨4,2,0⟩.$\n\nFirst, using the $3$ points we build $2$ vectors parallel to the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1} & =\\overset{\\to }{AP} \\\\  & =⟨3,-1,2⟩-⟨1,-2,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,1,1⟩ \\\\ {v}_{2} & =\\overset{\\to }{AQ} \\\\  & =⟨4,2,0⟩-⟨1,-2,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,4,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow,  we need to find the normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={v}_{1}\\times {v}_{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-5i+5j+5k \\\\  & =⟨-5,5,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-5,5,5⟩ & =⟨3,-1,2⟩\\cdot ⟨-5,5,5⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-5,5,5⟩ & =-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-5,5,5⟩ & =-10 \\\\ -5x+5y+5z & =-10 \\\\ -5x+5y+5z+10 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f3cdc898-7c65-52bc-9785-8f3da0b98b76"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f3cdc898-7c65-52bc-9785-8f3da0b98b76" :answer-field/id #uuid "f3cdc898-7c65-52bc-9785-8f3da0b98b76" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-88552711-7258-529e-8575-2c6ac297ae0d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-88552711-7258-529e-8575-2c6ac297ae0d" "answer-b5ddaec5-2f45-5d0e-8c08-e6549f59e357" "answer-4f5bbffd-b662-53da-9146-542052fb7f6e" "answer-8